<Legal title="Privacy policy" updated="October 26, 2026">
    <p>
        This privacy policy tells how Synnax Labs, Inc. ("Synnax Labs", "we", "us")
        collects, uses, shares, and protects personal information. It applies when you:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Visit our websites, such as{" "}
            <a href="https://www.synnaxlabs.com">www.synnaxlabs.com</a> and{" "}
            <a href="https://docs.synnaxlabs.com">docs.synnaxlabs.com</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
            Use the Synnax portal at{" "}
            <a href="https://portal.synnaxlabs.com">portal.synnaxlabs.com</a>, where you
            manage your account and licenses.
        </li>
        <li>Use Synnax Desktop.</li>
        <li>Contact us, or deal with us in sales, support, or events.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Synnax Labs is responsible for this information. If you have questions, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        The Synnax Core, Console, and Driver that you run on your own computers do not
        send us the data that you record. A Synnax Core checks its license on its own,
        with no connection to us. The Console app checks our website for updates.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Portal account</strong>: your name, email address, and password. If
            you log in with Google or Microsoft, we get your name, email address, and
            profile image from that account. We do not get your Google or Microsoft
            password.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Organization</strong>: the name of your organization, its members,
            their roles, and the email addresses of the people you invite.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Messages</strong>: what you send us in a contact form, a feedback
            form, or an email, such as your name, email address, company, and message.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Information about your machines and licenses</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>License records</strong>: the licenses of your organization, their
            terms and seats, and a log of license actions, with who did each action and
            when.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Machine names</strong>: the name that you give a machine when you
            activate a license. For Synnax Desktop, the host name of the computer.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Host fingerprints</strong>: one-way hashes of the hardware (MAC)
            addresses of the network interfaces of a computer. We get the hashes, not
            the addresses.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Renewals</strong>: when each Synnax Desktop computer first logged in
            and last renewed its license.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Synnax Desktop usage data</h3>
    <p>
        After you log in, Synnax Desktop can send usage data: launches, the type of each
        screen, clicks and recordings of the app window with all text masked, actions
        such as creating a channel, how long the built-in Core takes to start and how
        long it runs, why it stops, the size of the data that a reset erases, crash
        reports, and survey answers. Crash reports include the error message, which can
        name a channel or a device. Usage data is linked to the email address and ID of
        your account. Synnax Desktop does not send recorded data, channel values, or
        files. For the full list, see{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.synnaxlabs.com/reference/desktop/usage-data">
            Synnax Desktop usage data
        </a>
        .
    </p>
    <p>
        In the EU, the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland, Synnax Desktop asks for your
        consent at login, and sends usage data only if you agree. Everywhere else, it
        shows a notice at login, and usage data is on. You can turn it off at any time
        with the "Share usage data" switch in the app.
    </p>

    <h3>Information we collect automatically</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Website analytics</strong>: on docs.synnaxlabs.com, the pages you
            visit, your clicks, your browser and device type, and an identifier stored
            in your browser.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Search</strong>: the words that you search for in the documentation.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Logs</strong>: our servers and service providers record the IP
            address, browser, and time of each request, for security and to fix
            problems.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Cookies</strong>: the portal uses cookies to keep you logged in.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To make and run your account and organization.</li>
        <li>To issue, renew, and check licenses, and to count seats.</li>
        <li>
            To send service emails, such as invitations and warnings that a license will
            expire.
        </li>
        <li>To answer your messages and give support.</li>
        <li>To find and fix bugs, and to learn which features people use.</li>
        <li>To prevent abuse, such as too many license requests in a short time.</li>
        <li>To obey the law, and to protect our rights and the rights of others.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        We do not sell personal information. We do not share it for targeted
        advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
    <p>
        If the law of the EU, the EEA, the UK, or Switzerland applies to you, we process
        personal information on these bases:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Contract</strong>: to give you an account, licenses, and Synnax
            Desktop.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Consent</strong>: for Synnax Desktop usage data. You can withdraw
            consent at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Legitimate interests</strong>: for security, abuse prevention,
            website analytics, and to improve our products.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Legal obligation</strong>: when the law requires it.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Who we share information with</h2>
    <p>
        These service providers process personal information for us, under contracts
        that limit how they use it:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Clerk</strong>: portal accounts, login, and organizations.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>PostHog</strong> (US cloud): Synnax Desktop usage data and website
            analytics.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Resend</strong>: sends portal emails.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Vercel</strong>: hosts our websites and the portal.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Neon</strong>: stores portal records in a database.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Amazon Web Services</strong>: signs license keys. The signed data
            includes host fingerprints.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Formspree</strong>: receives contact and feedback forms.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Algolia</strong>: runs the documentation search.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Google and Microsoft get information only if you choose to log in with them. We
        can also share information when the law requires it, to protect our rights, or
        as part of a merger, sale, or similar change of our company.
    </p>

    <h2>5. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
        We are in the United States, and our service providers store information in the
        United States. When we transfer personal information from the EU, the EEA, the
        UK, or Switzerland, we use [TRANSFER MECHANISM, such as the standard contractual
        clauses or the Data Privacy Framework].
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Account and organization information</strong>: while your account is
            open. We delete it within [NUMBER] days after you ask us to.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>License records and fingerprints</strong>: for the life of the
            license and [NUMBER] years after it ends, for contracts, tax, and disputes.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Synnax Desktop usage data</strong>: [NUMBER] months. Recordings of
            the app window: [NUMBER] days.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Website analytics</strong>: [NUMBER] months.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Server logs</strong>: [NUMBER] days.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Messages</strong>: as long as we need them to answer you, and
            [NUMBER] years after.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. How we protect information</h2>
    <p>
        We encrypt connections to our services, limit who can get access to personal
        information, and keep the license signing key in a hardware key service. The
        portal gets only hashes of network addresses, never the addresses. No system is
        completely secure, so we cannot promise that information will never be lost or
        stolen.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you can have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Get a copy of the personal information we have about you.</li>
        <li>Correct information that is wrong.</li>
        <li>Delete your information.</li>
        <li>
            Get your information in a format that you can move to a different service.
        </li>
        <li>Object to, or limit, how we use your information.</li>
        <li>Withdraw your consent, with no effect on what we did before.</li>
        <li>Complain to your data protection authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Residents of California and other US states can have the right to know, correct,
        and delete their information, and to opt out of its sale or sharing. We do not
        sell or share personal information. We do not treat you differently when you use
        these rights.
    </p>
    <p>To use your rights:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            Email <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>. We
            can ask you to confirm who you are. We answer within one month, or within
            the time that your local law sets.
        </li>
        <li>
            To stop Synnax Desktop usage data, turn off "Share usage data" in the app.
        </li>
        <li>
            To remove a Synnax Desktop computer from your account, log it out on the
            Devices page of the portal.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
        Our services are not for people under 18. We do not knowingly collect
        information from them. If you think that we have such information, email us and
        we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>
        Our websites do not change what they do when a browser sends a Do Not Track
        signal.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        When we change this policy, we change the date at the top. If a change is
        important, we tell account holders by email before it applies.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:privacy@synnaxlabs.com">privacy@synnaxlabs.com</a>, or
        write to:
    </p>
    <p>
        Synnax Labs, Inc.
        <br />
        3064 Whitman Drive, Suite 400
        <br />
        Evergreen, CO 80439
        <br />
        United States
    </p>
</Legal>
